---
source: crates/quill-tui/tests/settings.rs
expression: outline(&shown)
---
== General (general, gearshape)
   keymap "Keys:": choice = mutt of vim "Vim" | mutt "Mutt"
     help: Keys of your own in keys.toml stay on top of either.
   notifications "New mail:": toggle "Show a notification when mail arrives" = false
   threads "Message list:": toggle "List the messages of a conversation together" = false
   web_reading "Reading:": toggle "Read mail in a web pane beside the list" = true
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Appearance (appearance, paintpalette)
   appearance "Appearance:": choice = system of system "System" | light "Light" | dark "Dark"
     help: System follows the Mac, and changes with it.
   theme_light "Light theme:": choice = light of dark "Dark" | light "Light" | terminal "Terminal"
   theme_dark "Dark theme:": choice = light of dark "Dark" | light "Light" | terminal "Terminal"
   font "Font:": font = ""
   font_size "Size:": number = 13 from 6 to 72 by 1, 1 places, points
     help: The font of Quill’s own window, and of an editor in it. In a terminal Quill has the terminal’s font.
   themes "Themes:": list
     row "Dark": Dark · comes with Quill [edit]
     row "Light": Light · comes with Quill · the theme in use [edit]
     row "Terminal": The terminal’s own colours · comes with Quill [edit]
     action edit "Edit…", of a row
     action delete "Delete…", of a row
     action import "Import…"
     empty: 
     help: Edit… changes a theme’s colours, and Quill is drawn in them as they are chosen. Saved under another name it is a new theme, and the one it was made from is left as it was. Themes made for Ghostty can be imported. Your own themes are files in the themes folder beside the settings file.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Accounts (accounts, at)
   accounts "": list
     row "Work": Microsoft 365, robin@example.com. Signs in with Microsoft. [sign_in, remove]
     row "Home": IMAP, robin@example.org. Signs in with a password. [edit, remove]
     action add "Add an Account…"
     action sign_in "Sign In…", of a row
     action edit "Edit…", of a row
     action remove "Remove…", of a row
     empty: No accounts yet.
     help: Edit… changes an account’s servers, the name it signs in with and its password. Removing an account takes it out of the settings file and the Keychain, and deletes the copy of its mail kept on this Mac. Mail on its server is not touched.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Composing (composing, square.and.pencil)
   editor "Write in:": choice = nano of builtin "Quill’s own editor" | vim "Vim" | nano "nano" | pico "Pico" | mg "mg"
     help: An editor other than Quill’s own is yours, with your own settings for it: Vim reads your vimrc. Takes effect when Quill is next opened. Until then messages are written in Quill’s own editor.
   editor_path "Program:": text = "/opt/homebrew/bin/nano"
     help: Left empty, Quill runs the nano it finds in the Mac’s own folders and then Homebrew’s. A whole path runs that program instead, such as /opt/homebrew/bin/nvim. Takes effect when Quill is next opened.
   format "Format:": choice = plain of markdown "Markdown, sent as formatted text" | plain "Plain text"
   reply_position "Replies:": choice = below of above "Above the quoted message" | below "Below the quoted message"
   spell_check "Spelling:": toggle "Check spelling as you type" = false
   undo_send_seconds "Undo send:": number = 30 from 0 to 4294967295 by 1, 0 places, seconds
     help: How long a sent message waits in the Outbox, where it can be taken back. 0 sends at once.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Keys (keys, keyboard)
   bindings "": list
     row "Next item or line": j, down [change]
     row "Previous item or line": k, up [change]
     row "Go to the top": =, home [change]
     row "Go to the bottom": *, end [change]
     row "Page down": space, pagedown [change]
     row "Page up": -, pageup [change]
     row "Open": enter [change]
     row "Close": q, ctrl-c [change]
     row "Quit": Q [change]
     row "Back, close or dismiss": i, esc, q [change]
     row "Focus the accounts pane": 1 [change]
     row "Focus the message list": 2 [change]
     row "Focus the reader": 3 [change]
     row "Focus the next pane or field": tab [change]
     row "Focus the previous pane or field": shift-tab [change]
     row "Show the accounts pane": \ [change]
     row "Zoom the focused pane": z, ctrl-z [change]
     row "Group or ungroup conversations": T [change]
     row "Web reading pane": w [change]
     row "Mark read or unread": N [change]
     row "Star or unstar": F [change]
     row "Show as HTML or as plain text": t [change]
     row "Open a link": o [change]
     row "Archive": e [change]
     row "Delete": d [change]
     row "Move to a folder": s [change]
     row "Copy to a folder": C [change]
     row "Put back": P [change]
     row "Snooze until a time": b [change]
     row "Select or unselect": x [change]
     row "Select a range": V [change]
     row "Select every message listed": ctrl-a [change]
     row "Search": /, cmd-f [change]
     row "Check for New Mail": G, ctrl-r, cmd-r [change]
     row "New folder…": + [change]
     row "Remove this empty folder from this Mac": _ [change]
     row "Show the account's folders": right [change]
     row "Hide the account's folders": left [change]
     row "Command palette": :, ctrl-k [change]
     row "List the attachments": v [change]
     row "Open in the browser": B [change]
     row "Load remote pictures for this message": L [change]
     row "Always load remote pictures from this sender": ctrl-l [change]
     row "Unsubscribe from this list": X [change]
     row "Run a hook on this message": | [change]
     row "Accept the invitation": y [change]
     row "Decline the invitation": n [change]
     row "Answer the invitation with maybe": M [change]
     row "Save the attachment": s [change]
     row "Open the attachment in its application": O [change]
     row "Write a new message": m [change]
     row "Reply": r [change]
     row "Reply to all": g [change]
     row "Forward": f [change]
     row "Send": cmd-enter, ctrl-x, ctrl-enter [change]
     row "Send at a time": cmd-L, ctrl-l [change]
     row "Save as a draft": cmd-s, ctrl-s [change]
     row "Attach a file": cmd-A, ctrl-t [change]
     row "Add blind copies (Bcc)": cmd-B, ctrl-o [change]
     row "Insert a template": cmd-T, ctrl-r [change]
     row "Write in Another Editor": cmd-E, ctrl-v [change]
     row "Go to the fields above the text": cmd-up [change]
     row "Go to the text": cmd-down [change]
     row "Show what the editor's keys do": cmd-/ [change]
     row "Spelling suggestions": cmd-G, ctrl-g [change]
     row "Go to the next misspelling": cmd-;, ctrl-y [change]
     row "Copy what is selected in the message being written": cmd-c [change]
     row "Cut what is selected in the message being written": cmd-x [change]
     row "Select all of the message being written": cmd-a [change]
     row "Undo the last move, deletion or send": U [change]
     row "Add an account": A [change]
     row "Sign in to an account": S [change]
     row "Edit this account…": E [change]
     row "Remove this account…": D [change]
     row "Stop Agents": Z a [change]
     row "Help for this context": ? [change]
     row "Keyboard shortcuts": K, f1 [change]
     action change "Change…", of a row
     action reset "Use the Default", of a row
     action reset_all "Reset All…", off
     empty: 
     help: The keys are the Mutt keys (General), with your own on top. A key changed here is written to keys.toml, beside the settings file, and holds at once. A key with ⌘ works in the app and not in a terminal, which keeps ⌘ for itself.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Privacy (privacy, hand.raised)
   remote_images "Remote pictures:": choice = never of ask "Ask for each message" | never "Never load them"
     help: Pictures and other content a message would fetch from the internet. Asked for, nothing is fetched until you say so for a message or for its sender.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Agents (agents, sparkles)
   commands "Shell commands:": toggle "Let quill’s commands work on the mail" = true
   mcp "MCP:": toggle "Serve agents over MCP while Quill is running" = false
     help: An agent’s program is given this command to reach Quill: quill mcp
   organize "They may:": toggle "Organize mail: mark, move, archive, snooze" = true
   delete "": toggle "Delete mail: to the trash, never for good" = true
   draft "": toggle "Write drafts" = true
   send "": toggle "Send mail" = false
   notify "Tell me:": choice = changes of changes "When they change or send mail" | sends "When they send mail" | none "Nothing of what they do"
     help: An agent connecting over MCP is always said. What they do is always said in Quill’s window, and kept in the log.
   recent "Lately:": list
     action copy_mcp "Copy MCP Command"
     action stop "Stop Agents"
     empty: Nothing has been changed from outside Quill’s window.
     help: What commands and agents changed last; quill log in a shell has all of it, and quill undo takes a change back. Stop Agents switches both ways in off at once and takes back their mail that has not gone. These settings stop an agent that has been misled. They are not a wall against a program that runs as you and means harm: keeping an eye on your agents is still yours to do.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
== Storage (storage, internaldrive)
   cache_gb "Keep up to:": number = 0.5 from 0 to any by 1, 2 places, GB of downloaded mail
     help: Past that the oldest downloaded copies are let go, and fetched again when next opened. 0 is no limit. Mail of a POP3 account is never cleared. Takes effect when Quill is next opened. Until then Quill keeps to 5 GB.
   more: Rules and saved searches are set in the settings file. Hooks and templates are files beside it.
